From: ghywel <gareth.herbert@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:03:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rule30WedgeBridge, Rule30SeparatorBridge,
 Rule30SeparatorEquivalences, Rule30SEPToPeriodTwo: state the relations to Q01
 proved in Rule30SeparatorQ01

The module docs and the Rule30SEPToPeriodTwo catalogue row said that no implication is proved between
SEP, RW or BWH and Q01. They now name what Rule30SeparatorQ01 proves (Q01 implies SEP, SEP is Q01 on
free bits with no two adjacent whites, BWH is equivalent to exact-width death bounds and implies Q01),
that Q01 is equivalent to mortality of the auxiliary frontier, and what stays open (SEP or RW implying
Q01, Q01 implying RW or BWH).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
